<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Stensby</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1238</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Stensby was concluded in 1238 at Stensby in Zealand between King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valdemar-ii-of-denmark">Valdemar II of Denmark</a> and the Livonian Order, mediated by the papal legate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-of-modena">William of Modena</a>. It returned northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>, with Rävala, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harju-county">Harjumaa</a> and Virumaa, to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jarva-county">Järvamaa</a> stayed with the Order, settling the rivalry that had followed the conquest of Estonia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-stensby.jpg" alt="Treaty of Stensby" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. 藏骨集团 assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_Estonian_counties.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
